# Clone: "You may have this creature enter as a copy of any creature on the battlefield." (CR 614.1c, 707.2) On turn 1
# Bot1 casts Ornithopter, then Clone for Black Lotus's {U}{U}{U} and Mox Sapphire's {U}, and accepts. The Ornithopter is
# the lone creature, so it is copied without asking which (the Mox, an artifact, is no candidate). Clone is then an
# Ornithopter in every copiable value: the name, a colorless 0/2 Artifact Creature - Thopter with flying (its own blue,
# Shapeshifter and 0/0 are gone), so it does not die as a 0/0.

[Bot1 Deck]
Ornithopter
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Clone
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Clone.Cast
Bot1.Accept
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Ornithopter; Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Types = Artifact; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Subtypes = Thopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Colors = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Keywords = Flying
